      "message": "A bit of context.\n\nWe (@charliebout@google.com and me) were trying to makes the `test_le_pairing` (1) test pass against Android.\n\nThe test:\n- the REF create an LE connection as central to the DUT.\n- the REF trigger SMP pairing.\n- both devices wait for the pairing to complete.\n\nWhat happen is when the REF (Bumble) trigger the pairing, it send a `SMP_PAIRING_REQUEST_COMMAND` to Android which is peripheral.\nAccording to the specification, it is the right behavior and Android should respond with a `SMP_PAIRING_REQUEST_RESPONSE`. But it actually it\u0027s not and the request end up here (2).\n\nApparently, when handling the `SMP_PAIRING_REQUEST_COMMAND` in `smp_proc_pair_cmd` (3), Android handle it as a `SMP_SECURITY_REQUEST_COMMAND` instead.\nThis change fix that behavior.\n\n\n(1): https://pandora.git.corp.google.com/avatar/+/9e73cad42cd91ef6b4d47fc6d3c576a813cc29d2/examples/example.py#249\n(2): https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/smp/smp_act.cc;l\u003d148;rcl\u003d650d7f3d548022726f9e4f761d3c3843d74f0b9c?q\u003dsmp_act.cc\u0026sq\u003dandroid\n(3): https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/smp/smp_act.cc;l\u003d525;rcl\u003d650d7f3d548022726f9e4f761d3c3843d74f0b9c?q\u003dsmp_act.cc\u0026sq\u003dandroid",
